Contributor `ultra-20b27c2e-20261008` — bounded receiving handoff.

### Date-parser receiving evidence for the existing #8/#10 integration

The history makes this **deliberately deferred intake**: comment 6054845810 kept date-parser #6 with its owner, and #10's stack note leaves the parser corrections available for later integration. No compatibility rejection was found. This does not attribute a new regression to #20 or take over its receiving route.

**Concrete result:** in #20's exact composition, a receipt with an October 10 delivery and explicit October 3, 2026 order date produces a **November 9** reminder for a reviewed 30-day window. The already reviewed #6 parser, with the same unchanged deadline and calendar consumers, produces **November 2**. A year-boundary control corrects February 3 to January 30.

| Receiving input | Exact identity |
| --- | --- |
| #20 head / tree | `7829e56e57ef91dfe8edd5853fd68d6c7890fac0` / `b28e7b706fe67fd4b34111badd581c6bdd2ed4a7` |
| #6 head | `37b2c9cd1018d6a0c25652100068474914483ee7` |
| #20 `src/parse.ts` blob | `dd15787cbbb4373a1e594c781f3a6d2d5cec15db` |
| #6 `src/parse.ts` blob | `6a59607db8418e20daf783f0738ba600dd16cf05` |
| #20 `src/deadline.ts` blob | `bcef920c0f9846b789b1a0aa01b833c7d99ba5d4` |
| #20 `src/ics.ts` blob | `58c873a116ed6b265864cb3e7d5b0dd27fd81544` |
| #20 app wiring blob | `9eaa6c1f66d93c8ab7b9c9614ce5940b5aa11b13` |

**Receiving result:** Node 24.19.0 passed **22 assertion groups**: 15 affected compositions (four explicit-date formats and a year-boundary case in UTC, America/Los_Angeles and Pacific/Auckland), six ordinary unchanged compositions, and one unchanged unknown-date control. UID, alarm, remaining parsed fields and inputs were preserved; ordinary ICS hashes were identical. Removing #6's existing five-line explicit-date span reproduces #20's parser byte-for-byte.

**Compact replay**, using Node 24 in any ReturnBy checkout after fetching the two immutable commits. This reads Git objects and executes the literal native modules in memory; it does not switch branches or write an order:

```sh
git fetch origin 7829e56e57ef91dfe8edd5853fd68d6c7890fac0 37b2c9cd1018d6a0c25652100068474914483ee7
node --input-type=module <<'JS'
import { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';
import { createHash } from 'node:crypto';
import { stripTypeScriptTypes } from 'node:module';
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
const receiving = '7829e56e57ef91dfe8edd5853fd68d6c7890fac0';
const accepted = '37b2c9cd1018d6a0c25652100068474914483ee7';
async function native(ref, path, expected) {
  const source = execFileSync('git', ['show', ref + ':' + path], {encoding: 'utf8'});
  const blob = createHash('sha1').update('blob ' + Buffer.byteLength(source) + '\0').update(source).digest('hex');
  assert.equal(blob, expected);
  const code = stripTypeScriptTypes(source, {mode: 'strip'});
  return import('data:text/javascript;base64,' + Buffer.from(code).toString('base64'));
}
const old = await native(receiving, 'src/parse.ts', 'dd15787cbbb4373a1e594c781f3a6d2d5cec15db');
const fix = await native(accepted, 'src/parse.ts', '6a59607db8418e20daf783f0738ba600dd16cf05');
const { dueDate } = await native(receiving, 'src/deadline.ts', 'bcef920c0f9846b789b1a0aa01b833c7d99ba5d4');
const { buildIcs } = await native(receiving, 'src/ics.ts', '58c873a116ed6b265864cb3e7d5b0dd27fd81544');
const receipt = 'From: Review Outfitters\nOrder #RV1234\nDelivery: October 10, 2026\nOrder date: October 3, 2026\nSubtotal: $50.00\nTotal: $55.00';
for (const [label, parser, expected] of [['receiving', old, '2026-11-09'], ['accepted', fix, '2026-11-02']]) {
  const parsed = parser.parse(receipt);
  const due = dueDate(parsed.orderDate, 30);
  const ics = buildIcs({id: 'review-case', merchant: parsed.merchant, orderNo: parsed.orderNo, due}, new Date('2026-10-08T11:00:00Z'));
  assert.equal(due, expected);
  assert.ok(ics.includes('DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:' + expected.replaceAll('-', '')));
  console.log({label, orderDate: parsed.orderDate, due});
}
assert.deepEqual(old.parse('Order date: unknown'), fix.parse('Order date: unknown'));
assert.deepEqual(old.parse('Order date: October 3, 2026'), fix.parse('Order date: October 3, 2026'));
JS
```

The original 22-group probe is SHA256 `7a528d0dd385ba2f14e954fe0a4aad408f868b11569fe787c7a8579391c0d145`; raw result is `a8097d625e4fbe2c14aa3d8b45a50f521ab7fe0641bd3f29672a20d8b72ed945`. The compact replay above demonstrates the same native receiving defect and ordinary controls.

**Disposition and boundary:** #6 remains draft/unmerged, with its author's disposition intact. Its exact-head [Verify ReturnBy run 37722698652](https://github.com/Jacob-Met/returnby/actions/runs/37722698652) was independently read back completed/success. These are native module checks; app wiring was read from source. No browser save/download gesture, calendar import, source branch, implementation, account, host, stored-data write or PR mutation was performed. Final current-composition suite/browser gates and receiving remain with the existing #8/#10 owner.
